{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a photoredox-catalyzed cascade radical cyclization for the synthesis of indole-fused 1,4-diazepinones. Using aroyl chlorides as acyl radical precursors and Ir(ppy)3 as a photocatalyst under blue LED irradiation, the method converts N-indolyl phenylacrylamides into polycyclic structures with axial chirality. The reaction proceeds via radical addition to the alkene followed by intramolecular cyclization at the indole C2-position, yielding diastereomeric products in high yields.",
